                    {
                        "sense_id": "0867db25-33d6-331b-8761-4c91403875be",
                        "entry_id": "dcb0adaf-f5ec-35f5-94ec-501162131463",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To curdle; to turn, as milk; to coagulate."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d5eaf87-a594-4eab-909b-4b994d25119d",
                                "sense_id": "0867db25-33d6-331b-8761-4c91403875be",
                                "text": "to posset the blood"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0ea8cd47-bd2e-432e-817a-434c4de818a7",
                                "sense_id": "0867db25-33d6-331b-8761-4c91403875be",
                                "text": "[…] And with a ſodaine vigour it [Hebenon, a poison] doth poſſet / And curd, like Aygre [vinegar] droppings into Milke, / The thin and wholſome blood: […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "26e933a2-120e-3c08-b2a3-3d6dd6fed35c",
                        "entry_id": "dcb0adaf-f5ec-35f5-94ec-501162131463",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To treat with possets; to pamper."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb1ff5f8-328c-4c1b-96d2-2f5629a6257c",
                                "sense_id": "26e933a2-120e-3c08-b2a3-3d6dd6fed35c",
                                "text": "Nevertheless, as she laid him in bed and posseted him, how frail and fragile he looked!"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5432188b-b0c3-32b9-942f-fdb3d794f460",
                        "entry_id": "dcb0adaf-f5ec-35f5-94ec-501162131463",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To vomit up curdled milk."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "of a baby"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b0f362d4-331e-4058-a1d7-7b6e368a709d",
                                "sense_id": "5432188b-b0c3-32b9-942f-fdb3d794f460",
                                "text": "Some babies never posset at all. Others do so with surprising ease, and this can be quite a cause of concern to parents."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce5e4ad1-b2cb-4a10-9b07-24f23ef0c72f",
                                "sense_id": "5432188b-b0c3-32b9-942f-fdb3d794f460",
                                "text": "All babies posset."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "587c3426-e377-4dbc-9ee8-2f307693b3c5",
                                "sense_id": "5432188b-b0c3-32b9-942f-fdb3d794f460",
                                "text": "It's also common for babies to 'posset' - bring up small amounts of milk after a feed - and to vomit occasionally."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
